0..77 Comment "// A case at a family of two indices omits an arm that is apart at one index."
78..80 Comment "//"
81..155 Comment "// Each branch binds one path for each index. The path runs from the index"
156..232 Comment "// that its constructor states to the index of the scrutinee. An omitted arm"
233..283 Comment "// must eliminate a path whose two ends are apart."
284..286 Comment "//"
287..364 Comment "// The lowering chooses that path by the constructors at the heads of the two"
365..442 Comment "// ends. The checker refuses an omitted arm whose ends are apart at no index."
443..484 Comment "// The pathological twin holds that case."
485..487 Comment "//"
488..503 Comment "// - see: #3402"
505..545 Comment "// The naturals the dimensions count in."
